  "notes": "Governmental funds cash basis: 126,098 + 862,004 - 937,584 + 197,668 - 197,668 - 19,357 (loan repayments printed under Other financing sources (uses)) = 31,161. Governmental 'Taxes' are property tax per the Statement of Activities. Governmental spending is listed by object only (no function). Business-type (modified cash) statement lines from the proprietary funds Statement of Revenues, Expenses and Changes in Net Position (p7), fund columns summed per row (no Total column): 2,257,595 + 878,662 + 8,589 - 868,944 - 12,605 - 24,565 = 2,238,732; nonoperating lines are printed below the operating totals (outside_printed_total). Proprietary statements have no total column; proprietary Statement of Cash Flows Total column used for 'proprietary'. Balance sheet from the government-wide Statement of Net Position (business-type capital assets and debt). Detail: the 'General Fund' budgetary comparison schedule covers all governmental funds by department (pp9-12; zero-actual budget lines omitted); loan repayments are printed among its charges to appropriations, so they stay expenditure there. No business-type detail lines (as FY2024: no proprietary detail schedules; proprietary statement columns not used as detail). Read pages 1-12 of 12"
